---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About Tipitaka Editions in Markdown: mission, architecture, and the 5 canonical Pāḷi editions preserved in open Markdown format."
  lang="en"
>
  <main style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem;">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem;">
      <a href="/" style="color: var(--primary-color); text-decoration: none;">Home</a>
      <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">/</span>
      <span style="color: var(--text-secondary);" aria-current="page">About</span>
    </nav>

    <header style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 0.75rem;">
        About Tipitaka in Markdown
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">
        Preserving, structuring, and comparing canonical Theravāda Buddhist literature across 5 international traditions in open, version-controlled Markdown.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Mission & Overview -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 1rem;">
        🌱 Project Mission
      </h2>
      <p style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        The <strong>Pāḷi Tipiṭaka</strong> represents the foundational corpus of early Buddhist teaching, preserved for millennia through oral recitation and later inscribed onto palm-leaf manuscripts across South and Southeast Asia. Over the 19th and 20th centuries, major national and international scholarly councils printed authoritative editions—each reflecting subtle historical, orthographical, and regional readings.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <strong>Tipitaka Editions in Markdown</strong> was founded to bring these monumental editions into the modern open-source text ecosystem. By converting each tradition into standardized, structured <strong>Markdown (<code>.md</code>)</strong> files and hosting them in publicly accessible, version-controlled Git repositories, we provide students, scholars, practitioners, and software developers with an unencumbered foundation for reading, collating, and analyzing the Dhamma.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Why Markdown? -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 1rem;">
        📄 Why Plain Text Markdown?
      </h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        <div style="background: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            ⏳ Future-Proof &amp; Resilient
          </h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">
            Plain text files remain readable indefinitely without requiring proprietary software, specific database engines, or operating systems. They will outlive proprietary platforms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            🔍 Git Version-Controlled
          </h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">
            Every single line, variant, and punctuation mark is tracked in Git. Discrepancies and improvements can be reviewed via pull requests and diffs with full provenance.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            🛠️ Universal Interoperability
          </h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">
            Markdown can be transformed into HTML, PDF, EPUB, static sites, or fed directly into natural language processing pipelines, AI models, and offline reading apps.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The 5 Editions -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 1rem;">
        🏛️ The 5 Editions Represented
      </h2>
      <p style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        The project preserves 5 primary international editions, each converted deterministically and hosted in its own repository:
      </p>

      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;">
        <!-- WTK -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary-color); padding-left: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left-width: 4px;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0;">
              🌟 World Tipiṭaka Edition (WTK / tipitaka2500) — Base Reference
            </h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/tipitaka2500" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--primary-color); text-decoration: none;">tipitaka-md/tipitaka2500 ↗</a>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-body); margin: 0.5rem 0 0;">
            The 40-volume Roman-script World Tipiṭaka Edition (<em>Mahāsaṅgīti Tipiṭaka Buddhavasse 2500</em>, updated 2020 edition), converted from the digital edition at <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka2500/tipitaka2500.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--primary-color);">tipitaka2500/tipitaka2500.github.io</a> (<a href="https://tipitaka2500.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--primary-color);">tipitaka2500.github.io</a>). Converted into 20,190+ individual files organized by volume, vagga, and sutta, it serves as the canonical base text for collation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- PTS -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid #165b48; padding-left: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left-width: 4px;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0;">
              🇬🇧 Pali Text Society (PTS)
            </h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/pts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #165b48; text-decoration: none;">tipitaka-md/pts ↗</a>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-body); margin: 0.5rem 0 0;">
            The pioneering European Roman-script critical edition founded by T.W. Rhys Davids in 1881. Converted from <a href="https://github.com/INDOLOGY/GRETIL-mirror" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #165b48;">INDOLOGY/GRETIL-mirror</a> (originally digitized by the Dhammakaya Foundation in collaboration with PTS and hosted at <a href="https://gretil.sub.uni-goettingen.de/gretil.html#Pali" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #165b48;">GRETIL</a>). Structured into 372 Markdown files split by sutta, chapter, and vagga with preserved PTS volume and page citation anchors.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- BJT -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid #85677b; padding-left: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left-width: 4px;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0;">
              🇱🇰 Buddha Jayanthi Tripitaka Series (BJT)
            </h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/buddha-jayanthi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #85677b; text-decoration: none;">tipitaka-md/buddha-jayanthi ↗</a>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-body); margin: 0.5rem 0 0;">
            The official 57-volume Sri Lankan Government commemorative edition sponsored under the Buddha Jayanthi commemoration (1956–1989). Converted from the digital proofread JSON edition maintained by <a href="https://github.com/pathnirvana/tipitaka.lk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--primary-color);">pathnirvana/tipitaka.lk</a> and transliterated from Sinhala script to standard Roman (IAST Pali) using Aksharamukha, covering all 285 files (28,967 printed BJT pages) across Vinaya, Sutta, Abhidhamma, and Aṭṭhakathā with preserved page numbering and footnotes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- CST -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid #695d08; padding-left: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left-width: 4px;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0;">
              🇲🇲 Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (CST)
            </h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/cst" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #695d08; text-decoration: none;">tipitaka-md/cst ↗</a>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-body); margin: 0.5rem 0 0;">
            The authoritative Sixth Buddhist Council text sanctioned by an international council of Theravāda elders in Yangon (Myanmar, 1954–1956) and digitized by the Vipassana Research Institute (VRI). Converted deterministically from <a href="https://github.com/VipassanaTech/tipitaka-xml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--primary-color);">VipassanaTech/tipitaka-xml</a> across 217 books covering Mūla, Aṭṭhakathā, and Ṭīkā into structured Markdown with footnotes and variant readings.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Siam Rath -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid #96254a; padding-left: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left-width: 4px;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0;">
              🇹🇭 Royal Thai Edition (RTE / Syāmaraṭṭha)
            </h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/siam-rath" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #96254a; text-decoration: none;">tipitaka-md/siam-rath ↗</a>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-body); margin: 0.5rem 0 0;">
            The prestigious 45-volume Royal Thai Syāmaraṭṭha Tepiṭakaṃ published under the patronage of King Prajadhipok (Rama VII, 1925–1928). Extracted from <a href="https://github.com/kit119/D-tipitaka" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--primary-color);">kit119/D-tipitaka</a> SQL source and transliterated from Thai script to IAST Pali Roman using Aksharamukha, covering all 45 volumes, 21,915 printed pages, and 17,090 variant footnotes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Technical Architecture -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 1rem;">
        ⚡ Architecture &amp; Design Principles
      </h2>
      <ul style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0; color: var(--text-body);">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          <strong>Dynamic Client-Side Rendering:</strong> Texts are fetched and rendered directly in the user’s browser from raw GitHub repository files or high-speed CDNs, without using the browser's HTTP cache for these requests. Upstream caches may still affect freshness.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          <strong>Original Integrity:</strong> Raw Markdown files are never modified for web presentation. Formatting adaptations (such as paragraph flow and footnote anchoring) occur dynamically in memory during rendering.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          <strong>Zero Lock-in:</strong> Every text can be downloaded as an untouched <code>.md</code> file or viewed on GitHub with a single click.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          <strong>Online Reading:</strong> An internet connection is required to fetch texts. Downloaded Markdown files can be read offline.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Project Maintainer & License -->
    <section style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-top: 2rem; margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-emphasis); margin: 0 0 1rem;">
        👤 Project Maintainer &amp; Dedication
      </h2>
      <p style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Created and maintained by <strong>Chris Tham</strong> (<a href="mailto:chris@christham.net" style="color: var(--primary-color);">chris@christham.net</a>).
      </p>
      <p style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        All structuring, scripts, and documentation developed for this project are released under the <strong>Creative Commons Zero (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication</strong>. You are completely free to copy, modify, distribute, and perform the work, even for commercial purposes, without asking permission.
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a
          href="/guide.html"
          class="btn-primary"
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; color: #fff; background-color: var(--primary-color);"
        >
          <span>📘 Read the Quick Guide →</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="/reader.html?book=1V"
          class="btn-secondary"
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-body); background-color: var(--bg-secondary);"
        >
          <span>📖 Start Reading</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
